    <item>
      <title>About</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/about/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/ashish-pal-website/about/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h1 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;About&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;about&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#about&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Prof. Ashish Pal is an Assistant Professor in the Department of Civil Engineering at the Indian Institute of Technology Bombay.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;His research lies at the intersection of structural engineering, scientific computing, sensing technologies, and artificial intelligence. His work focuses on developing mechanics-informed intelligent systems for structural health monitoring, digital twinning, and resilient infrastructure management.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Research Interests&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;research-interests&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#research-interests&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Structural Health Monitoring&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Digital Twins of Civil Infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Physics-Informed Machine Learning&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Scientific Computing&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Computer Vision-Based Structural Monitoring&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Vibration-Based Damage Detection&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Drone-Based Infrastructure Monitoring&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;Uncertainty Quantification&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;System Identification of Dynamical Systems&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Research Vision&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;div id=&#34;research-vision&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;    &lt;span&#xD;&#xA;        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none&#34;&gt;&#xD;&#xA;        &lt;a class=&#34;text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#research-vision&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &lt;/span&gt;&#xD;&#xA;    &#xD;&#xA;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xD;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The long-term goal of the research is to develop intelligent infrastructure systems capable of autonomous sensing, interpretation, prediction, and decision support by integrating mechanics, data, and machine intelligence.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
